{"id": "EUVD-2026-71417", "enisaUuid": "e96c6040-fe68-330c-b2a8-d6409341e454", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: asus: fix missing hid_is_usb() check\n\nto_usb_interface() can only be used on a hid_device whose parent is really\nUSB; uhid can create devices that identify as being on BUS_USB, but don't\nactually have a USB parent.\nFix the use of to_usb_interface() without a hid_is_usb() check.\n\nI have verified that it is currently possible to trigger a kernel splat due\nto this bug in an ASAN build, and that this commit fixes the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:12:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:43:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdb2e0a2a359e473ca5619e35adee89028697239", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b5debb6252cd1e2b6c7adf8f95761a0e743d2cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ddc2f5913bec7a846544d51a8f7a8119573b2a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee883906cf6685d753af9c2d2ca9fd6f63197726", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/02bf61dfb44f17ec187d1da1a82495951bbd12df"], "aliases": ["GHSA-682h-7hxw-p7mc", "CVE-2026-80774"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2607d171-5b62-3133-bc65-7b4dc028feb7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.35 <6.12.108"}, {"id": "2d53e0de-3d14-3641-9505-3e4dddef10d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2e888085-d1b2-31b2-9b08-3155e2a86f19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3d4b7330-23f8-3164-9b03-095361fe9357", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15.4 <6.16"}, {"id": "61f1cd32-044f-3fdd-ac97-324e6c9fb260", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "00e005c952f74f50a3f86af96f56877be4685e14 <02bf61dfb44f17ec187d1da1a82495951bbd12df"}, {"id": "81405110